      "type": "text",
      "x": 1480,
      "y": 539.0,
      "width": 247.52,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "STATUS  \u2014  the state machine",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "STATUS  \u2014  the state machine",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el111",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1428150522,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 372587780,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1480,
      "y": 574.0,
      "width": 530.4,
      "height": 243.75,
      "text": "                      :commit             indexed\n   AWAITING_UPLOAD  ------------>  PENDING  --------->  LIVE\n          |                           |\n          | no commit in 24 h         +--> FAILED  unsupported type\n          v                           |             no text layer\n      ABANDONED                       |             (needs OCR)\n      row + parts swept               +--> FAILED  retries exhausted\n\n   the Indexer acts on PENDING and on NOTHING else.\n   that single rule does two jobs:  it makes it safe to create\n   the row 60 s before the bytes land, and it stops the\n   status = LIVE write-back from looping back through Debezium.\n\n   lane A rows are born PENDING  \u2014  the body came with the\n   request, so there is nothing left to wait for.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "                      :commit             indexed\n   AWAITING_UPLOAD  ------------>  PENDING  --------->  LIVE\n          |                           |\n          | no commit in 24 h         +--> FAILED  unsupported type\n          v                           |             no text layer\n      ABANDONED                       |             (needs OCR)\n      row + parts swept               +--> FAILED  retries exhausted\n\n   the Indexer acts on PENDING and on NOTHING else.\n   that single rule does two jobs:  it makes it safe to create\n   the row 60 s before the bytes land, and it stops the\n   status = LIVE write-back from looping back through Debezium.\n\n   lane A rows are born PENDING  \u2014  the body came with the\n   request, so there is nothing left to wait for.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el112",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#6741d9",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1700113407,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1989259376,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 88.4,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "EXTRACTION",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "EXTRACTION",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el113",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1723943247,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 364725392,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 1912,
      "width": 579.6,
      "height": 262.5,
      "text": "in scope    txt  md  csv  html    ->  decode  (strip tags for html)\n            pdf                   ->  pypdf, page by page\n            docx                  ->  python-docx\n            anything else         ->  FAILED, unsupported type\n\nnot doing   OCR  \u00b7  passage chunking  \u00b7  the ES attachment processor\n\nwhy not the attachment processor: Tika would parse on the DATA NODES,\nburning the CPU that has to answer searches in under 500 ms. one bad\nPDF would slow every query routed to that node. keep parsing in a\nworker you can kill and scale on its own.\n\nthere is NO extraction size cap. a 100 MB PDF runs the same code in\nthe same lane  \u2014  streaming to disk keeps memory flat either way.\nonly the consumer config differs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "in scope    txt  md  csv  html    ->  decode  (strip tags for html)\n            pdf                   ->  pypdf, page by page\n            docx                  ->  python-docx\n            anything else         ->  FAILED, unsupported type\n\nnot doing   OCR  \u00b7  passage chunking  \u00b7  the ES attachment processor\n\nwhy not the attachment processor: Tika would parse on the DATA NODES,\nburning the CPU that has to answer searches in under 500 ms. one bad\nPDF would slow every query routed to that node. keep parsing in a\nworker you can kill and scale on its own.\n\nthere is NO extraction size cap. a 100 MB PDF runs the same code in\nthe same lane  \u2014  streaming to disk keeps memory flat either way.\nonly the consumer config differs.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el114",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 682281554,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 730160160,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 335.92,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "S3 LAYOUT  &  WHAT ACTUALLY TOUCHES S3",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "S3 LAYOUT  &  WHAT ACTUALLY TOUCHES S3",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el115",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 545625653,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 118321418,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 1912,
      "width": 562.8,
      "height": 280.0,
      "text": "{tenant}/{doc_id}/raw     the original bytes, immutable\n{tenant}/{doc_id}/text    extracted text, derived, rebuildable\n\nreal S3 API calls:\n   CreateMultipartUpload   :negotiate,  > 100 MB only\n   CompleteMultipartUpload :commit,     stitches the parts\n   HEAD                    :commit,     verify it is really there\n   GET  /raw               Indexer,     when the row has an s3_key\n   PUT  /text              Indexer,     after extraction\n\npresigning is NOT in that list. it is a local HMAC over a canonical\nrequest  \u2014  zero network calls. that is why :negotiate can mint 50\npart URLs in microseconds, and why the 5-100 MB tier shows no arrow\nto S3 at negotiate time at all.\n\nthe bytes themselves never pass through Ingest on any tier.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "{tenant}/{doc_id}/raw     the original bytes, immutable\n{tenant}/{doc_id}/text    extracted text, derived, rebuildable\n\nreal S3 API calls:\n   CreateMultipartUpload   :negotiate,  > 100 MB only\n   CompleteMultipartUpload :commit,     stitches the parts\n   HEAD                    :commit,     verify it is really there\n   GET  /raw               Indexer,     when the row has an s3_key\n   PUT  /text              Indexer,     after extraction\n\npresigning is NOT in that list. it is a local HMAC over a canonical\nrequest  \u2014  zero network calls. that is why :negotiate can mint 50\npart URLs in microseconds, and why the 5-100 MB tier shows no arrow\nto S3 at negotiate time at all.\n\nthe bytes themselves never pass through Ingest on any tier.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el116",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 649187325,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1998679711,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2210,
      "width": 247.52,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "CONFIG THAT ACTUALLY MATTERS",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CONFIG THAT ACTUALLY MATTERS",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el117",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 627813882,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2037347502,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2242,
      "width": 571.1999999999999,
      "height": 192.5,
      "text": "batch by BYTES, not count       a 100 MB doc becomes a batch of one\nmax.poll.interval.ms = 900000   otherwise slow extraction looks like\n                                a dead consumer: Kafka rebalances,\n                                the batch is retried, and nothing\n                                ever finishes\nephemeral-storage: 4Gi          room for concurrent temp files, or\n                                the kubelet evicts the pod\nAbortIncompleteMultipartUpload after 7 days\n                                abandoned parts are BILLED and do\n                                not appear in the object listing\nsweep AWAITING_UPLOAD older than 24 h  ->  ABANDONED",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "batch by BYTES, not count       a 100 MB doc becomes a batch of one\nmax.poll.interval.ms = 900000   otherwise slow extraction looks like\n                                a dead consumer: Kafka rebalances,\n                                the batch is retried, and nothing\n                                ever finishes\nephemeral-storage: 4Gi          room for concurrent temp files, or\n                                the kubelet evicts the pod\nAbortIncompleteMultipartUpload after 7 days\n                                abandoned parts are BILLED and do\n                                not appear in the object listing\nsweep AWAITING_UPLOAD older than 24 h  ->  ABANDONED",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el118",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
